# Binary names exposed on the host as shims into the `dev` toolbox container
# (image ghcr.io/samcday/workstation-config/toolbox:main); see install.sh in
# this directory. One name per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Known `toolbox run` caveats (verified against toolbox src/cmd/run.go and
# src/pkg/utils/utils.go):
# - cwd, exit status and stdin/stdout/stderr (incl. a TTY) are preserved, so
#   the shims are drop-in replacements for normal use. One upstream wart:
#   toolbox 0.3 reports success when the tool itself exits 127.
# - Rust: the image ships Fedora's rust/cargo plus rustup. If you have run
#   rustup on the host, ~/.cargo/bin (shared via $HOME) likely precedes
#   ~/.local/bin in PATH and its binaries win over these shims.
# - toolbox forwards only an allowlist of host env vars: COLORTERM, DISPLAY,
#   HOME, HIST*, LANG, SHELL, SSH_AUTH_SOCK, TERM, WAYLAND_DISPLAY,
#   XAUTHORITY, XDG_*. `FOO=1 rg ...` on the host does NOT make FOO visible
#   to rg, and EDITOR is not forwarded either.
# - if the host cwd is outside $HOME (e.g. /tmp, /mnt), toolbox falls back to
#   $HOME inside the container with a notice on stderr: the shims are only
#   reliable under $HOME.
# - tools see argv[0] as their container path, so multi-call binaries need
#   one shim per name; keep one entry per name here.

bat
cargo
fzf
gcc
gh
go
just
jq
make
meson
ninja
node
npm
python3
rg
rustc
shellcheck
yamllint
yq
